.\" ###### Description ######################################################
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm print\-utf8
prints UTF\-8 strings in the console with options for indentation, centering,
and horizontal separators, and queries byte size, code\-point length, and
terminal display\-column width (ignoring ANSI escape sequences and accounting
for combining marks and wide CJK/Emoji glyphs).
.Pp
String and border arguments support standard backslash escape sequences
.Pq Ql \[rs]n , Ql \[rs]r , Ql \[rs]t , Ql \[rs]a , Ql \[rs]b , Ql \[rs]f , Ql \[rs]v , Ql \[rs]e , Ql \[rs]E , Ql \[rs]\[rs] , Ql \[rs]0ooo , Ql \[rs]xhh , Ql \[rs]uhhhh , No and Ql \[rs]Uhhhhhhhh .
Terminal dimensions are obtained from standard output,
.Pa /dev/tty ,
or the
.Ev COLUMNS
and
.Ev LINES
environment variables, falling back to 80x24 if unavailable.
.\" ###### Arguments ########################################################
.Sh ARGUMENTS
The following arguments and options are available:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Op Ar string
The UTF\-8 string to process (defaults to an empty string if omitted; multi\-line
modes
.Fl I
and
.Fl C
read lines from standard input instead).
.It Fl n | Fl \-newline
Append a trailing newline to the output (default: off).
.It Fl i Ar indentation | Fl \-indent Ar indentation
Pad the string with spaces to a field width of
.No | Ns Ar indentation Ns |
display columns. A negative value pads on the right (left\-justified text); a
positive value pads on the left (right\-justified text).
.It Fl c | Fl \-center
Center the string within the console width.
.It Fl I Ar indentation Ar left Ar right | Fl \-multiline\-indent Ar indentation Ar left Ar right
Reads up to 1024 lines from standard input, indents each line according to
.Ar indentation ,
and wraps each line with
.Ar left
and
.Ar right .
.It Fl C Ar left Ar right | Fl \-multiline\-center Ar left Ar right
Reads up to 1024 lines from standard input, centers and pads each line within
the console width (minus the display widths of
.Ar left
and
.Ar right ) ,
and wraps each line with
.Ar left
and
.Ar right .
.It Fl s Ar left Ar separator Ar right | Fl \-separator Ar left Ar separator Ar right
Generates a horizontal separator line consisting of
.Ar left ,
repeated occurrences of
.Ar separator
up to the target console width, and
.Ar right .
If
.Ar separator
has display width 0, a single space
.Pq Ql " "
is used instead.
.It Fl x Ar console\_width | Fl \-columns Ar console\_width
Set the target console width (up to 4096 columns) for
.Fl c ,
.Fl C ,
and
.Fl s .
For
.Ar console\_width Ns =0 ,
the detected console width (or 80, if unknown) is used.
For
.Ar console\_width Ns <0 ,
the detected console width (or 80, if unknown) plus
.Ar console\_width
(subtracting the offset) is used. Default: 0 (current console width).
.It Fl b | Fl \-size
Print the size in bytes of the string without ANSI control sequences.
.It Fl l | Fl \-length
Print the length in Unicode code points of the string without ANSI control sequences.
.It Fl w | Fl \-width
Print the display width in terminal columns of the string without ANSI control sequences.
.It Fl a | Fl \-size\-length\-width
Print the byte size, code\-point length, and display width of the string without ANSI control sequences.
.It Fl t | Fl \-terminal\-info
Print the current width and height of the console (checking standard output,
.Pa /dev/tty ,
and
.Ev COLUMNS Ns / Ns Ev LINES ,
or returning
.Ql 80 24
if unavailable).
.It Fl h | Fl \-help
Prints the program's command\-line parameters and exits.
.It Fl v | Fl \-version
Prints the program version and exits.
.El
.\" ###### Exit status ######################################################
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The
.Nm
tool exits with 0 on success, and >0 in case of an error.
.\" ###### Examples #########################################################
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -bullet
.It
print\-utf8 \-\-newline \-\-center \[dq]This line is centered in console width!\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-\-newline \-\-columns 80 \-\-center \[dq]This line is centered in 80 columns!\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-\-newline \-\-center \[aq]\[rs]x1b[38;2;241;71;29mThis line is centered!\[rs]x1b[0m\[aq]
.It
figlet \[dq]$(date +\[dq]%y\-%m\-%d\[dq])\[dq] | print\-utf8 \-\-newline \-\-multiline\-indent 64 \[dq]< \[dq] \[dq] >\[dq]
.It
figlet \[dq]$(date +\[dq]%y\-%m\-%d\[dq])\[dq] | print\-utf8 \-\-newline \-\-multiline\-indent \-64 \[dq]< \[dq] \[dq] >\[dq]
.It
figlet \[dq]This is a test!\[dq] | print\-utf8 \-\-newline \-\-multiline\-center \[dq]<🏁\[dq] \[dq]🏁>\[dq]
.It
figlet \[dq]This is another test!\[dq] | print\-utf8 \-x \-8 \-n \-C \[dq]<🏁\[dq] \[dq]🏁>\[dq]
.It
figlet \[dq]Right\[dq] | print\-utf8 \-n \-I +72 \[dq]😀\[dq] \[dq]😀\[dq]
.It
figlet \[dq]Left\[dq]  | print\-utf8 \-n \-I \-72 \[dq]😀\[dq] \[dq]😀\[dq]
.It
date +\[dq]%d. %m.  %Y %H:%M:%S\[dq] | figlet \-w 128 | print\-utf8 \-n \-C \[dq][🕑\[dq] \[dq]🕑]\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-n \-c \[dq]😀😀😀 This line is centered in console width! 😀😀😀\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-n \-x 80 \-c \[dq]😀😀😀 This line is centered in 80 columns! 😀😀😀\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-\-indent \-32 \[dq]Left: \[dq] && echo \[dq]1234\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-\-indent +32 \[dq]Right: \[dq] && echo \[dq]1234\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-\-newline \-\-separator \[dq]<*\[dq] \[dq]=\[dq] \[dq]*>\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-\-columns 80 \-\-newline \-\-separator \[dq]<*\[dq] \[dq]=\[dq] \[dq]*>\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-n \-s \[dq]<💻😀\[dq] \[dq]=\[dq] \[dq]😀💻>\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-\-width \[dq]Test\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-\-width \[dq]Test äöü\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-b \[dq]😀 Test 😀\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-l \[dq]😀 Test 😀\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-w \[dq]😀 Test 😀\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-a \[dq]😀 Test 😀\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-\-terminal\-info
.It
print\-utf8 \-n \-s \[dq]\[rs]e[1;34m╔\[dq] \[dq]═\[dq] \[dq]╗\[rs]e[0m\[dq]\~;
.br
date +\[dq]%d. %m. %Y %H:%M:%S\[dq] | figlet \-w 128 | \[rs]
.br
print\-utf8 \-n \-C \[dq]\[rs]e[1;34m║🕑\[rs]e[1;31m\[dq] \[dq]\[rs]e[1;34m🕑║\[rs]e[0m\[dq] ;
.br
print\-utf8 \-n \-s \[dq]\[rs]e[1;34m╚\[dq] \[dq]═\[dq] \[dq]╝\[rs]e[0m\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-n \-s \[dq]\[rs]e[1;31;5m█\[dq] \[dq]▀\[dq] \[dq]█\[rs]e[0m\[dq]\~;
echo \[dq]ERROR  1234\[dq] | figlet \-w 128 | print\-utf8 \-n \-C \[dq]\[rs]e[1;31;5m█\[rs]e[25m\[dq] \[dq]\[rs]e[5m█\[rs]e[0m\[dq]\~;
.br
print\-utf8 \-n \-s \[dq]\[rs]e[1;31;5m█\[dq] \[dq]▄\[dq] \[dq]█\[rs]e[0m\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-n \-s \[dq]\[rs]e[1;31;40;5m█\[dq] \[dq]▀\[dq] \[dq]█\[rs]e[0m\[dq]\~;
.br
echo \-e \[dq]Software Failure.   Press left mouse button to continue.\[rs]nGuru Meditation #00000004.48454C50\[dq] | \[rs]
.br
print\-utf8 \-n \-C \[dq]\[rs]e[1;31;40;5m█\[rs]e[25m\[dq] \[dq]\[rs]e[5m█\[rs]e[0m\[dq]\~;
.br
print\-utf8 \-n \-s \[dq]\[rs]e[1;31;40;5m█\[dq] \[dq]▄\[dq] \[dq]█\[rs]e[0m\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-n \-x 44 \-s \[dq]\[rs]e[1;32m╒\[dq] \[dq]═\[dq] \[dq]╕\[rs]e[0m\[dq]\~;
.br
ls / | print\-utf8 \-n \-\-multiline\-indent \-42 \[dq]\[rs]e[1;32m│\[rs]e[34m\[dq] \[dq]\[rs]e[1;32m│\[rs]e[0m\[dq]\~;
.br
print\-utf8 \-n \-x 44 \-s \[dq]\[rs]e[1;32m╘\[dq] \[dq]═\[dq] \[dq]╛\[rs]e[0m\[dq]
.It
print\-utf8 \-\-help
.It
print\-utf8 \-h
.It
print\-utf8 \-\-version
.It
print\-utf8 \-v
.El
